This should help identify the underlying cause.

This error usually means that you are trying to access a property on an object that is `undefined`. Check the data returned by `fetchCascades`. If you’re expecting an array, ensure it always returns a valid structure. Modify `fetchCascades` to add error handling:

```javascript
const fetchCascades = () => {
    // Ensure data is defined
    const data = simulateDataFetch();
    if (!data) throw new Error('Data fetch failed');
    return data;
